From e5e8cc2b90569ae08d9bb1b217c062024618cfd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 01:44:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] JavaScriptCore: compares, tests, new objects, polymorphic
 calls and scope variables in the 68k template JIT

- Fix: after a call through the JIT's call fast path (since stage J4),
  the interpreter's sp was left at the callee's frame, not at the
  caller's frame bottom as restoreStackPointerAfterCall leaves it. A
  garbage collection then took the caller's slots below that sp for dead
  and cleared them (sanitizeStack): values became empty and could crash
  the engine. The return point now restores sp.
- ===, !==, == null, != null and their jumps, jtrue and jfalse, and
  <, <=, >, >=, ==, != as values (int32s) get their own code for every
  kind of value the interpreter handles without a call: int32s,
  booleans, undefined and null, and cells by identity. Doubles, strings
  compared by content and objects that act as undefined take the
  template. jeq_ptr and jneq_ptr compare the whole value.
- put_by_id gets its own code for cached transitions (a new property on
  an object, as in object literals and constructors), with the prototype
  chain check where the cache holds one.
- Calls: a call site whose cache has gone polymorphic searches the
  stub's call slots (by callee, or by executable for closures) and
  enters the callee's compiled code directly; call_ignore_result
  (a call whose result is unused) gets the same code as call.
- resolve_scope, get_from_scope and put_to_scope get their own code for
  global variables and properties, global let and const, and closure
  variables, for the resolve type the site's cache holds, with the
  interpreter's checks (var injection, read-only and TDZ checks,
  watchpoint sets, the write barrier).
- Loop register copies cover all of these.

Real-page tests (68k instructions, against 0034): a tokenizer runs 1.7x
fewer, an event/store app 1.4x, a virtual DOM diff 1.3x, JSON handling
1.1x, HTML templating 1.04x; closures 1.4x. The sp fix costs a plain
call two instructions (the calls test 2%). Lab tests correct6-8 check every value kind, polymorphic
calls, transitions, scopes and garbage collection against node.
